      "id": "claim_cc1574c733334712a4eee4073143f3b0",
      "statement": "An MCP binding's grant breadth is encoded in the resource-URL fragment (<endpoint> = whole endpoint, #server=<id> = one portal upstream server, #tool=a&tool=b = named tools only), with endpoint identity compared over the whole URL (path and query included, so /mcp and /mcp-v2 on one host are unrelated) and action-kind approval tags namespaced by exactly that identity; the generic connector refuses #server= as it is the portal connector's grammar.",
