      "id": "claim_cd7aa9c6994446ed868f3620bc2fed5b",
      "statement": "MCP bindings are owner-only: addObserver refuses unconditionally because MCP has no per-record authorization to consult — holding a connection to the same origin proves only that a person can authenticate, not that they may read what the gadget read on the owner's credentials — with the refusal message pointing at publishing a blueprint so each person connects their own account; writes remain allowed since writing back to the source server discloses nothing new.",
